1
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:07,120
intimated that he, too, had a few words to say.

2
00:00:07,120 --> 00:00:11,959
Like all of Napoleon's speeches, it was short and to the point.

3
00:00:11,959 --> 00:00:18,879
He, too, he said, was happy that the period of misunderstanding was at an end.

4
00:00:18,879 --> 00:00:23,360
For a long time there had been rumors, circulated, he had reason to think, by

5
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:28,079
some malignant enemy, that there was something subversive and

6
00:00:28,079 --> 00:00:33,000
even revolutionary in the outlook of himself and his colleagues.

7
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,479
They had been credited with attempting to stir up rebellion among the animals

8
00:00:36,479 --> 00:00:38,360
on neighboring farms.

9
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:41,559
Nothing could be further from the truth.

10
00:00:41,559 --> 00:00:47,000
Their sole wish, now and in the past, was to live at peace and in normal

11
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,920
business relations with their neighbors.

12
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:56,520
This farm, which he had the honor to control, he added, was a cooperative enterprise.

13
00:00:56,520 --> 00:01:02,719
The title deeds, which were in his own possession, were owned by the pigs jointly.

14
00:01:02,719 --> 00:01:08,159
He did not believe, he said, that any of the old suspicions still lingered. But

15
00:01:08,159 --> 00:01:12,799
certain changes had been made recently in the routine of the farm, which should

16
00:01:12,799 --> 00:01:16,559
have the effect of promoting confidence still further.

17
00:01:16,559 --> 00:01:20,440
Hitherto the animals on the farm had had a rather foolish custom of addressing

18
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:24,479
one another as comrade.

19
00:01:24,479 --> 00:01:27,079
This was to be suppressed.

20
00:01:27,079 --> 00:01:31,680
There had also been a very strange custom, whose origin was unknown, of

21
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:38,920
marching every Sunday morning past the boar's skull, which was nailed to a post in the garden.

22
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:41,680
This, too, would be suppressed.

23
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:44,719
And the skull had already been buried.

24
00:01:44,719 --> 00:01:50,680
His visitors might have observed, too, the green flag which flew from the masthead.

25
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:55,719
If so, they would perhaps have noted that the white hoof and horn with which

26
00:01:55,719 --> 00:01:59,840
it had previously been marked had now been removed.

27
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:04,719
It would be a plain green flag from now onwards.

28
00:02:04,719 --> 00:02:11,760
He had only one criticism, he said, to make of Mr. Pilkington's excellent and neighborly speech.

29
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:18,040
Mr. Pilkington had referred throughout to Animal Farm.

30
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:24,840
He could not, of course, know, for he, Napoleon, was only now for the first time announcing it,

31
00:02:24,840 --> 00:02:29,520
that the name Animal Farm had been abolished.

32
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:37,440
Henceforth, the farm was to be known as the Manor Farm, which, he believed, was its correct and

33
00:02:37,440 --> 00:02:39,200
original name.

34
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:44,719
>> Gentlemen, I will give you the same toast as before, but in a different form.

35
00:02:44,719 --> 00:02:49,600
Fill your glasses to the brim, gentlemen. Here is my toast.

36
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:52,879
To the prosperity of the Manor Farm.

37
00:02:52,879 --> 00:02:58,799
>> There was the same hearty cheering as before, and the mugs were emptied to the dregs.

38
00:02:58,799 --> 00:03:04,360
But, as the animals outside gazed at the scene, it seemed to them that some

39
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:07,000
strange thing was happening.

40
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,920
What was it that had altered in the faces of the pigs?

41
00:03:10,920 --> 00:03:15,559
Clover's old, dim eyes flitted from one face to another.

42
00:03:15,559 --> 00:03:21,239
Some of them had five chins, some had four, some had three.

43
00:03:21,239 --> 00:03:25,879
But, what was it that seemed to be melting and changing?

44
00:03:25,879 --> 00:03:30,239
Then, the applause having come to an end, the company took up their cards and

45
00:03:30,239 --> 00:03:36,399
continued the game that had been interrupted. And the animals crept silently away.

46
00:03:36,399 --> 00:03:40,040
But, they had not gone 20 yd when they stopped short.

47
00:03:40,040 --> 00:03:43,760
An uproar of voices was coming from the farmhouse.

48
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:46,920
They rushed back and looked through the window again.

49
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:50,559
Yes, a violent quarrel was in progress.

50
00:03:50,559 --> 00:03:57,799
There were shoutings, hangings on the table, sharp, suspicious glances, furious denials.

51
00:03:57,799 --> 00:04:02,399
The source of the trouble appeared to be that Napoleon and Mr. Pilkington had

52
00:04:02,399 --> 00:04:06,399
each played an ace of spades simultaneously.

53
00:04:06,399 --> 00:04:10,559
12 voices were shouting in anger, and they were all alike.

54
00:04:10,559 --> 00:04:14,600
No question now what had happened to the faces of the pigs.

55
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:19,840
The creatures outside looked from pig to man, and from man to pig, and from pig

56
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:21,360
to man again.

57
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:25,440
But, already it was impossible to say which was which.
